# The rain cloud is uploaded once; the vertex shader advances every drop.
import scene_character_types.dl
import ../../packages/dynlex-ui/ui/scene_rotations.dl
import rain_motion.dl

class:
    patterns:
        website Farm weather
    members:
        landscape as a pointer to website Farm landscape
        object as a pointer to UI scene object

to get [the website Farm rain mesh]:
    set drop to a UI cylinder mesh with top 1.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 6 sides capped true
    set rotation to the UI scene rotation from direction (a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0) to direction (a new vector with x -0.05, y 0.3 and z 0.0)
    set length to the square root of ((0.05 * 0.05) + (0.3 * 0.3))
    set matrix to a UI scene matrix at (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) oriented rotation scaled (a new vector with x 0.009, y length and z 0.009)
    set transform to a UI scene transform from matrix
    set vertices to an empty list of UI mesh vertex
    set indices to an empty list of a 32 bit unsigned integer
    loop index from 0 to 600:
        set phase to ((index % 53) as a floating-point number) / 53.0
        set seed to phase * 9.0
        set center to a new vector with x ((the sine of (index * 54.3)) * 11.0), y seed and z ((the sine of (index * 21.7)) * 11.0)
        set base to the length of vertices
        for each vertex in drop's vertices:
            set position to (the UI scene position of (the UI mesh position of vertex) through transform) + center
            set normal to the UI scene normal of (the UI mesh normal of vertex) through transform
            # All vertices of a drop carry its seed height, so wrapping moves it whole.
            append UI mesh vertex at position normal normal uv seed 0.0 to vertices
        for each item in drop's indices:
            append ((base + (item as an integer)) as a 32 bit unsigned integer) to indices
    set result to a UI scene mesh taking vertices vertices and indices indices
    free vertices
    free indices
    return result

to get [website Farm weather in] {a pointer to website Farm landscape:landscape}:
    set result to storage for one slot initialized with (a new website Farm weather)
    set result's landscape to landscape
    set material to a UI scene material with color (UI ink 201 224 221) roughness 1.0 metalness 0.0
    set material's unlit and material's double sided to true
    set material's depth write to false
    set material's opacity to 0.6
    set material's flags to 3 as a 32 bit unsigned integer
    set model to a website Farm scene model using (the website Farm rain mesh) colored material casting shadow false
    set result's object to a website Farm object named "rain" using model in landscape
    set result's object's visible and result's object's pickable to false
    return result

to get [refresh website Farm weather] {a pointer to website Farm weather:weather} [at amount] {floating-point number:rain}:
    set visible to rain > 0.002
    set changed to weather's object's visible != visible
    set weather's object's visible to visible
    return changed

to [close website Farm weather] {a pointer to website Farm weather:weather}:
    remove website Farm scene object (weather's object) from (weather's landscape)
    destroy the value at weather
    deallocate weather
